    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds **Pairing-based BDHKE (BLS12-381)** as a peer to the legacy secp256k1 BDHKE protocol in NUT-00, with batch verification via a Fiat-Shamir weighted multi-pairing. Companion changes across the related NUTs introduce the new v3 keyset (version byte \\`02\\`) end-to-end:\r\n\r\n- **NUT-00** — new \\`# Pairing-based BDHKE (BLS12-381)\\` section covering variables (G1/G2/Fr), \\`hash_to_curve_G1\\` (RFC 9380 random-oracle suite with Cashu DST), multiplicative blinding protocol, single-proof pairing verification \\`e(C, G2) == e(Y, K)\\`, and batch verification with the full Fiat-Shamir transcript and equation. Legacy secp256k1 section renamed to \\`# Legacy secp256k1 based BDHKE\\` and version-gated.\r\n\r\n- **NUT-01** — public key serialization broadened: \\`00\\`/\\`01\\` keysets use compressed secp256k1 (33 B / 66 hex); \\`02\\` keysets use compressed BLS12-381 G2 (96 B / 192 hex).\r\n\r\n- **NUT-02** — new \\`#### Keyset ID V3\\` subsection: same algorithm as V2 with version byte \\`02\\` and G2 hex pubkeys in the preimage. V3 is now listed first as the current version.\r\n\r\n- **NUT-12** — scoped to secp256k1 keysets only. For v3 keysets, mints **MUST NOT** include \\`dleq\\` in \\`BlindSignature\\` responses and wallets **MUST NOT** include \\`dleq\\` in \\`Proof\\` objects; verification uses pairing equality.\r\n\r\n- **NUT-13** — V3 secret derivation row added: identical HMAC-SHA256 derivation to V2, with the blinding factor reduced modulo \\`BLS_FR_ORDER\\` (BLS12-381 G1 group order) instead of \\`SECP256K1_N\\`. Code samples parameterised on \\`scalar_order\\` to keep the spec terse.\r\n\r\n- **tests/00, 02, 13** — canonical test vectors: round-trip vector for \\`hash_to_curve_G1\\` / blind / sign / unblind on secret \\`\"test_message\"\\` with \\`r=3\\`, \\`a=2\\` (matching the pinned values in both reference implementations); two V3 keyset IDs (\\`02ce4c47…\\` unit-only, \\`02b53239…\\` with input_fee_ppk + final_expiry); a V3 derivation vector at counter=2 exercising the Fr-reduction branch.\r\n\r\nThe wire shape of \\`BlindedMessage\\` / \\`BlindSignature\\` / \\`Proof\\` and the V4 CBOR token format remain unchanged — only the byte-widths and curve identity of the \\`B_\\` / \\`C_\\` / \\`C\\` fields change, dispatched by the keyset version byte.\r\n",
